<title>INDIA: POLL-India L&amp;T 6-mth net seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-India L&amp;T 6-mth net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian engineering and construction giant Larsen &amp; Toubro Ltd (L&amp;T) is expected to report a 4.0 percent rise in net profit in the first half of fiscal 1997/98 (April-March), a Reuter poll consensus said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sales are seen advancing 19.5 percent to 28.2 billion rupees from 23.6 billion in the first half of 1996/97, according to 18 leading brokerages and securities houses.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>LARSEN &amp; TOUBRO ----PAT seen up 4.0%, sales 19.5%</p>
<p>Average		2,090.56  2,010.00    28,231.31  23,620.00</p>
<p>High		   2,564.00		  31,777.00</p>
<p>Low		    1,500.00		  25,236.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk +91-22-265-9000</p>
